    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1133">

                <pb facs="0815" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/54.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have sent to Sir Lionel
                    Garden the telegram from our Consul at Tampico, a paraphrase of which I handed
                    to you yesterday; and have added that as the oil wells in that district are
                    close together, and the British companies owning some of them employ United
                    States citizens, it would be quite impossible to draw any distinction of British
                    or American nationality between either wells or employees: and that all sympathy
                    would be alienated both here and elsewhere if these properties were
                    destroyed.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
